How it works:\
run_leximin.R grabs data from the \'91data\'92 folder, and run the leximin script from the \'91R\'92 folder.\
\
In the data folder, the example folders are named such that the last part of it will be the suggested panel size.\
In the files, \'91categories.csv\'92 and \'91respondents.csv\'92, you will see the format of the csv required. 
\f1\b Currently, the column names needs to be exactly the same
\f0\b0  as this example
\f1\b  for the algorithm to work.\
\

\f0\b0 To run this piece of code, you can go to a terminal and you need to change directory to this current folder. \
\
\
The command format is:\
\
\cb2 Rscript run_leximin.R DATA_DIR OUTPUT_CSV PANEL_SIZE ROUNDS PANEL_OUTPUT_CSV\cb3 \
